/// Dashboard/API credential. Deliberately a DIFFERENT credential from a lead
/// source's ingest token: an ingest token is pasted into a third party's UI and
/// lives in their logs, while an API key can read the whole tenant. Rotating one
/// must never break the other.
///
/// Hashed rather than encrypted, because we only ever verify a presented key and
/// never reproduce it. Unsalted SHA-256 is correct here: the key is 192 bits of
/// CSPRNG entropy, so there is no dictionary to attack and bcrypt would only add
/// latency to every request.
model api_keys {
  id              String        @id @db.Uuid
  organization_id String        @db.Uuid
  name            String        @db.VarChar(100)
  key_hash        String        @unique @db.VarChar(64)
